  "articleBody": "A wobbly bedroom handrail isn't just annoying; it's a safety hazard! If your handrail isn't as solid as it should be, it usually boils down to a few key issues with how it was installed or the materials used. The biggest culprit is often improper anchoring into the wall. If the screws aren't hitting studs, or if the anchors used aren't appropriate for the wall material – like plasterboard or drywall – the rail won't be able to bear much weight and will start to loosen over time. \n\nAnother reason could be the wall material itself. Weaker substrates need specific plugs or screws designed to provide a secure hold. If the wrong type was used, or if they weren't installed correctly, the rail will never feel truly firm. Sometimes, it's also a matter of simply not having enough mounting points or not distributing the load effectively. For folks in places like Littleton, Highlands Ranch, or Lone Tree, if you're noticing your handrail is moving, it’s a good idea to have a professional take a look. We can assess the wall structure, ensure proper fastening, and make sure your handrail provides the reliable support you need for fall prevention or mobility assistance. Don't risk a fall; get it checked out!",
